  <data name="kryptonWrapLabel1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Issue #4496: Office 2024 ribbon. The selected tab is an underline, groups have no boxes, and File is text. 
Switch Blue, Silver, White, grays, and Black, including dark and light modes. Microsoft 365 Blue keeps the folder-tab chrome. 
Home has two groups and a dialog launcher. Table Design is a contextual tab. File opens the backstage.
 Compact ribbon (#4533) lays those same groups on one row for every ribbon shape: icon and text, then icons only as the form narrows. 
Group captions and group boxes hide. Each shape keeps its own tabs. Arrow place chooses under the groups, the end of the groups, or the tab row. Switching eases the groups area. 
The arrow is optional. Narrow the window until ... appears at the end of the row, then click it for the commands that did not fit." + "Issue #4552: double-click File closes the form. 
A single click only opens the backstage. Beveled edges and gaps between groups are optional. Bevel size and group gap are pixels at 96 DPI. A gap of zero keeps one card. 
Context titles in the title bar are optional for Office 2024 and stay off until you turn them on. Microsoft 365 still shows them. 
Tab marks can be a straight line or a pill-shaped line under the label. An optional glow can be turned on.</value>
